Using a machine or VM with Docker installed (for example github code spaces).
Also ensure you have imported the requirements from requirements.txt.
---
1) ensure you are in the right directory:
open a terminal window and enter 'cd client' to change to the client directory.
---
2) run the docker compose file
in the same terminal type 'docker-compose up' to start Docker.
this should initialise a rabbitMQ container in Docker.
---
3) wait for Docker to finish initialising.
---
4) open port 8080 in a web browser.
(in visual studio code this can be done through the ports tab => hover over port 8080 -> click the globe icon)
---
5) in your browser window that pops up on port 8080, you should see a rabbitMQ login screen.
---
6) log into RabbitMQ using username 'guest' and password 'guest'.
---
7) this should take you to the rabbitMQ dashboard.
---
8) right click __main__.py and click run.
---
9) right click smart_meter_app.py and click run.
---
10) steps 8 and 9 should have started the server and started a client.
---
11) wait for readings to come through. logs for both can be seen in the consoles.